s":["His family history is notable for two siblings diagnosed with cystic fibrosis."]},{"sid":46450,"type":"social_history","lines":["He plans to have a child with a woman from the general population who has no known family history of cystic fibrosis."]},{"sid":46451,"type":"other_studies","lines":["Genetic screening confirms he is healthy with no clinical evidence of cystic fibrosis, but his carrier status is unknown."]},{"sid":46452,"type":"assessment","lines":["Cystic fibrosis is an autosomal recessive disorder caused by mutations in the CFTR gene, leading to thick, viscous secretions and recurrent pulmonary infections.","The carrier frequency for CFTR mutations in the general U.S. population is 1/25."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":11062,"date":"2022-01-15","type":"ed","dept":"Emergency Medicine","attending":"Dr. David Chen","cc":"Brought to the emergency department by his roommate due to erratic behavior.","order":2,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[5682],"sections":[{"sid":46453,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Brought to the emergency department by his roommate due to erratic behavior."]},{"sid":46454,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient is a 27-year-old male with Schizotypal Personality Disorder diagnosed in January 2020 and Bipolar I Disorder currently managed with lithium carbonate and lamotrigine, who presents with acute behavioral changes.","Over the past 3 days, he has been barely sleeping and working nonstop on what he describes as a \u201cworld-changing invention.\u201d He has been unusually talkative, jumping between topics, and spent thousands of dollars on gadgets online.","He also insists that his professors are watching him through his devices to steal his work."]},{"sid":46455,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Schizotypal personality disorder (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Homozygous Normal CFTR Genotype (Daughter) (diagnosed 2021-07-15)","- Bipolar I Disorder","","The roommate reports that the patient had a similar episode a year ago and had to be hospitalized."]},{"sid":46456,"type":"psh","lines":["- None"]},{"sid":46457,"type":"medications","lines":["Home Medications:","- Lithium carbonate 300 mg PO BID","- Lamotrigine 100 mg PO daily"]},{"sid":46458,"type":"allergies","lines":["No known drug allergies"]},{"sid":46459,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Father: Bipolar I Disorder","- Maternal uncle: Schizotypal personality traits (undiagnosed)","- Mother: Major depressive disorder"]},{"sid":46460,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never smoker.","Alcohol: Occasional social use (1-2 drinks per month).","Occupation: Graduate student in Electrical Engineering."]},{"sid":46461,"type":"labs","lines":["Urine drug screen is negative."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":11063,"date":"2025-01-15","type":"ed","dept":"Emergency Medicine","attending":"Dr. Sarah Kim","cc":"Brought to the emergency department by his roommate due to escalating behavioral changes over the past 10 days.","order":3,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[5810],"sections":[{"sid":46462,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Brought to the emergency department by his roommate due to escalating behavioral changes over the past 10 days."]},{"sid":46463,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient is a 30-year-old male with Bipolar I Disorder and Schizotypal Personality Disorder, on lithium and lamotrigine, returning three years after a prior ED admission for similar symptoms.","The roommate says the patient has been sleeping only 1\u20132 hours per night, is constantly talking, often jumping between topics, and has been impulsively spending large amounts of money online.","He recently claimed he has developed a device that allows him to \u201ccommunicate with satellites,\u201d despite no background in engineering.","He believes government agents are now tracking him through his phone."]},{"sid":46464,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Schizotypal personality disorder (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Homozygous Normal CFTR Genotype (Daughter) (diagnosed 2021-07-15)","- Bipolar I Disorder with Psychotic Features (diagnosed 2022-01-15)","- Bipolar I Disorder","","His medical and psychiatric history is unremarkable."]},{"sid":46465,"type":"psh","lines":["- None"]},{"sid":46466,"type":"medications","lines":["Home Medications:","- Lithium carbonate 300 mg PO BID","- Lamotrigine 100 mg PO daily"]},{"sid":46467,"type":"allergies","lines":["No known drug allergies"]},{"sid":46468,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Father: Bipolar I Disorder","- Maternal uncle: Schizotypal personality traits (undiagnosed)","- Mother: Major depressive disorder"]},{"sid":46469,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never smoker.","Alcohol: Occasional social use (1-2 drinks per month).","Occupation: Graduate student in Electrical Engineering."]},{"sid":46470,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On examination, the patient is restless and speaking rapidly with tangential thoughts.","He displays pressured speech and an irritable affect but is cooperative and oriented."]},{"sid":46471,"type":"labs","lines":["Urine toxicology is negative."]},{"sid":46472,"type":"assessment","lines":["After admission, his speech remains rapid and mood remains elevated, and his psychotic beliefs persist."]},{"sid":46473,"type":"plan","lines":["Within 5 days of starting inpatient treatment with mood stabilizers and antipsychotics, his mood and thought process begin to normalize.","At 3-week follow-up, the patient is euthymic with no residual psychotic symptoms."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":11060,"date":"2025-01-15","type":"ed","dept":"Emergency Medicine","attending":"Dr. James Patterson","cc":"Brought to the emergency department by his roommate due to sudden onset of severe neck pain, facial tightness, and difficulty moving his eyes.","order":4,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[5796],"sections":[{"sid":46474,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Brought to the emergency department by his roommate due to sudden onset of severe neck pain, facial tightness, and difficulty moving his eyes."]},{"sid":46475,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient is a 30-year-old male with established diagnoses of Bipolar I Disorder and Schizotypal Personality Disorder who returns to the emergency department on the same day as his discharge from a week-long inpatient psychiatric admission for acute mania with psychotic features.","Earlier in the day, he had been discharged from the inpatient unit after being prescribed a new medication to help stabilize his mood and prevent recurrence of his symptoms.","The patient states that approximately 5 hours after taking his first dose at home, he noticed a \u201cweird pulling\u201d sensation in his jaw and stiffness in the back of his neck.","Over the next hour, the pain worsened and his eyes \u201crolled up\u201d without his control.","His roommate became concerned when the patient was unable to straighten his head and appeared increasingly distressed, prompting transport to the hospital.","The roommate confirms that the new medication is a high-potency antipsychotic.","The patient denies any history of similar symptoms, previous antipsychotic use, recent alcohol or illicit drug use, and head trauma."]},{"sid":46476,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Schizotypal personality disorder (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Homozygous Normal CFTR Genotype (Daughter) (diagnosed 2021-07-15)","- Bipolar I Disorder with Psychotic Features (diagnosed 2022-01-15)","- Bipolar I Disorder","","During that admission, he had exhibited pressured speech, grandiosity, and disorganized behavior, including attempting to lecture strangers on \u201cunlocking the secrets of the universe\u201d in the middle of the night."]},{"sid":46477,"type":"psh","lines":["- None"]},{"sid":46478,"type":"medications","lines":["Home Medications:","- Lithium carbonate 300 mg PO BID","- Lamotrigine 100 mg PO daily"]},{"sid":46479,"type":"allergies","lines":["No known drug allergies"]},{"sid":46480,"type":"family_history","lines":["His family history is significant 